{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the manual-fix advice "or run ci.yml on the tag ref" can never produce a publish anymore**

With the r2 changes the second half of this recovery instruction is a no-op by construction:

- the publish job's `if` requires `github.event_name == 'push'` — a `workflow_dispatch` run of ci.yml on the tag ref skips publish (a rerun keeps the original event, so it can never fire later either);
- the r2 push-only selection (`push_run_of`) correctly refuses to treat that run as publishable, so the next daily reads the dispatch run, finds no push run, and (past grace) alarms `only non-push run(s) exist` — i.e. an operator who follows this exact advice makes the leg's diagnosis one step more confusing while fixing nothing.

The first half of the advice (`git push origin $tag --force`) is the fix that works — it creates a fresh push event and a publishable run. Suggest dropping the dispatch clause (or rewording to "re-push the tag — a fresh push event is the only way to get a publishable run"). Loud-alarm behavior is unaffected either way; this is runbook accuracy only.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md"}

